  "details": "On random instances of VRChat running, EasyAntiCheat will encounter a conflict with Windows Hyper-V as it detects Hyper-V as a virtual machine even when no virtual machines are running on the program, as it utilizes memory virtualization in the background. When EasyAntiCheat kills Hyper-V, memory corruption occurs, instantly crashing the system with the \"MEMORY_MANAGEMENT\" STOP error code. A fix does exist where disabling Hyper-V will fix the bug, but this means that Hyper-V cannot be in Windows at all while VRChat is installed. I've compiled the dump results into a text file for easier viewing.",
